@startuml
title The transition relation Turing actually declares: two entries, both leaving `q0`

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}

[*] --> q0 : a program is written\nin some configuration

state "q0\n`State::Q0`" as q0 #DCFCE7
state "q1\n`State::Q1`" as q1 #FEE2E2
state "halt\n`State::Halt`" as halt #FEF3C7
state "q <latex>n</latex>\n`State::Q(UInt32)`" as qn #E5E7EB

q0 --> q1 : **D_q0_0**  `turing.rs:186-187`\nread <latex>0</latex> / write <latex>1</latex>, move right\n`(Cf Q0 (Tp L Zero R))`\n`~> (Cf Q1 (shift_right L One R))`
q0 --> halt : **D_q0_1**  `turing.rs:188-189`\nread <latex>1</latex> / write <latex>1</latex>, stay\n`(Cf Q0 (Tp L One R))`\n`~> (Cf Halt (Tp L One R))`

note right of q0
  **Deterministic BY CONSTRUCTION, not by ordering.**
  The two left-hand sides differ in the head-symbol
  position: `Sym_Zero` against `Sym_One`. No
  configuration matches both. The engine itself
  performs no selection — it fires EVERY match
  in every iteration and merges the results
  (`dovetail/src/rules.rs:804-807`).
end note

note bottom of q1
  **DEAD END.** No rewrite has `Q1` on its
  left-hand side, so nothing can fire here.
  The machine stops in `q1` for the same
  reason it stops in `halt`: absence of a rule.
end note

note bottom of halt
  **NOT a reserved word.** `Halt` is an ordinary
  nullary `State` constructor (`turing.rs:151`).
  The macro, the runtime and the e-graph contain
  no notion of halting: `State_Halt` occurs 12
  times in the generated report, every one of them
  a mechanical op-enum / display / reconstruction
  arm plus `D_q0_1`'s right-hand side.
end note

note bottom of qn
  The paper's INDEXED state former, declared verbatim
  (`turing.rs:152`) and reachable only by writing it:
  `q 7u32` parses, prints and hashes. No transition
  mentions it, because the macro's pattern grammar has
  no literal form — `(Q 0u32)` cannot be written in a
  rewrite (`ast/src/pattern.rs:25-51`).
end note

@enduml
